  "term": "persecutory delusion",
  "definition": "A persecutory delusion is a fixed false belief that one is being plotted against, harmed, or watched by others. In the historical account here, it is described as part of a more organised suspicious mental state in which ordinary events are taken as signs of conspiracy and as referring personally to the affected person.",
